# License Header

## Guideline

- Start every code file, including test files, with the license header below.
- The header comes first in the code file, followed by a blank line.
{%- set line_comment_tokens = {
    'go': '//',
    'javascript': '//',
    'rust': '//',
    'typescript': '//',
    'powershell': '#',
    'python': '#',
    'shell': '#',
} %}
- The header text below is plaintext; when writing it into a code file, prefix every line with the file language's line-comment token:
{%- for language in languages %}
{%- if language in line_comment_tokens %}
  - `{{ language }}`: `{{ line_comment_tokens[language] }}`
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
- Formats without line comments (e.g. Markdown, JSON, YAML) don't carry the header.

{%- if license_header == 'Full' %}
{%- set notice_license = license|lower|replace('-or-later','')|replace('-only','') %}

## Full header

The header text for each code file is:

```
{% include 'licenses/' ~ notice_license ~ '-notice.jinja' -%}
```
{%- elif license_header == 'SPDX' %}

## SPDX identifier

The header text for each code file is:

```
{% include 'licenses/spdx-notice.jinja' -%}
```
{%- endif %}

